{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Take heed to yourselves.</b> Since you will be eating and satiated — take heed to yourselves lest you rebel, for a person rebels against the Holy One, blessed be He, only out of satiety, as it says: ״פֶּן תֹּאכַל וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבְקָרְךָ וְצֹאנְךָ יִרְבְּיֻן״ (Deuteronomy 8). And what does it say after it? ״וְרָם לְבָבֶךָ וְשָׁכַחְתָּ״." "<b>And you turn aside.</b> To depart from the Torah, and from that follows <b>and you serve other gods</b> — for once a person departs from the Torah he goes and clings to idolatry. And so David says: ״כִּי גֵרְשׁוּנִי הַיּוֹם מֵהִסְתַּפֵּחַ בְּנַחֲלַת ה׳ לֵאמֹר לֵךְ עֲבֹד וְגוֹ׳״ (I Samuel 26). And who told him so? Rather: since I am banished from occupying myself with Torah, I am close to serving other gods." "<b>Other gods.</b> For they are 'other' to their worshippers — he cries out to it and it does not answer him; it turns out alien to him (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:34.710433679Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}